dth=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"170\" r=\"148\" transform=\"scale(-1 1) translate(-600 0)  rotate(180 300 170)\"></circle> <line class=\"radius-line\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"448\" y2=\"169\"></line> <line class=\"vertical45\" x1=\"448\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"506\" y2=\"169\"></line> <line class=\"radius-45\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"406\" y2=\"66\"></line>  <line class=\"vertical45\" x1=\"406\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"406\" y2=\"166\"></line> <line class=\"vertical45\" x1=\"407\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"508\" y2=\"168\"></line> <line class=\"vertical45\" x1=\"302\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"65\"></line> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"330\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"470\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">tan θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"320\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">cos θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"420\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\" transform=\"rotate(90, 420, 128)\">sin θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"320\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"1.0em\" font-weight=\"bold\">θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"282\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">O</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"282\" y=\"9\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">y</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"407\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">P</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"370\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">sec θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"500\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">R</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"520\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">x</text></svg></div></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Graph 1</b>: The circle with radius 1 and the trigonometric segments built on it: cos θ, sin θ, tan θ and sec θ.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "### The other hypotenuse\n\n**Graph 1** shows the trigonometric relationships on the circle. Besides the right triangle whose hypotenuse is the radius 1, it contains a second, larger right triangle whose hypotenuse is the secant: the other hypotenuse of this text. We will focus on that segment and predict which values sec(θ) can take in the first quadrant we are studying.\n\n#### Isolating\n\nTo make this easier to see, we will isolate from **Graph 1** only the parts this study needs:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"atlasCircleContainer\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 200\" class=\"circle-draw\" id=\"svgcirctri0\">  <defs> <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"3\" markerHeight=\"3\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"> <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" /></marker></defs>  <line class=\"radius-line\" x1=\"200\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"348\" y2=\"169\"></line> <line class=\"vertical45\" x1=\"348\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"406\" y2=\"169\"></line> <line class=\"radius-45\" x1=\"200\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"306\" y2=\"66\"></line>  <line class=\"vertical45\" x1=\"307\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"408\" y2=\"168\"></line> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"230\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"370\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">tan θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"220\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"1.0em\" font-weight=\"bold\">θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"182\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">O</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"307\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">P</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"285\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">sec θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"400\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">R</text> </svg></div></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Graph 2</b>: The triangle from <b>Graph 1</b> isolated: there the secant is the hypotenuse.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### The definition\n\nThe segment we see in **Graph 2** also received a mathematical definition in an earlier text, where we manipulated trigonometric relationships and concluded that the secant is the reciprocal of the cosine (<htcite0>):",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "213a8932-84c2-4f72-9852-38368994d9a5",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Are we tangent to the planet?",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\" style=\"background-color: #FFFFFF;\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\" style=\"background-color: #FFFFFF;\"><p><math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mi>sec (θ)</mi><mn>=</mn><mfrac><mi>1</mi><mi>cos (θ)</mi></mfrac></math></p> <p class=\"desc\"><b>Formula 1</b>: Definition of the secant as the reciprocal of the cosine.</p></div></div></center>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### Curiosity\n\nA point made by Eric W. Weisstein deserves mention: this function originated almost alongside the tangent, but when another mathematical function — the logarithm — was discovered, its use declined (<htcite0>).\n\n#### The graph\n\nWe can build the graph of the secant from the tangent graph shown on the previous page (<htcite1>). There, we learned that the tangent is the sine divided by the cosine (**Formula 2**):",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "603c44f8-9b51-44f3-a538-9ddc6ba7be05",
                     "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
                     "page": "Secant",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cbce5f98-ad82-4995-b5f0-960554919dbd",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Our Position",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\" style=\"background-color: #FFFFFF;\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\" style=\"background-color: #FFFFFF;\"><p><math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mi>tan (θ)</mi><mn>=</mn><mfrac><mi>sin(θ)</mi><mi>cos (θ)</mi></mfrac></math></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Formula 2</b>: Definition of the tangent in terms of the sine and the cosine.</p></div></div></center>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "Comparing **Formulas 1 and 2**, we see that both divide by cos(θ); only the numerator changes: **Formula 1** divides 1 by cos(θ), while **Formula 2** divides sin(θ) by cos(θ). From this we can predict the graph of the secant:\n- When cos(θ) reaches its greatest value, 1, sec(θ) is also 1 — dividing 1 by 1 changes nothing;\n- As another *History Tracers* text notes, infinitely many numbers lie between 0 and 1 (<htcite0>). When cos(θ) shrinks from 1 toward 0, dividing 1 by a smaller and smaller positive number makes sec(θ) grow;\n- When cos(θ) = 0, the division is undefined, so sec(θ) has no value there.\n\nTo see this in a picture, look at **Graph 3**:",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "d06e24cb-52e8-4ff8-ae37-12052c91b187",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Limiting",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htChart\"><canvas aria-label=\"chart\" id=\"chartsec1\" style=\"width:30em !important; height:20em !important;\"></canvas></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Graph 3</b>: Graph of the secant function in the first quadrant: it starts at 1 and grows as θ increases. Graph created with the <htcite0> library.</div></p><script> htPlotSecant('chartsec1', 'theta (radians)', 'secant (θ)', 1);</script>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "6efe7632-faed-4080-a5aa-38463d43e6d7",
                     "text": "Chart JS",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "05",
                        "day": "30"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "To make the comparison with the tangent easier, we redraw it below:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htChart\"><canvas aria-label=\"chart\" id=\"charttan2\" style=\"width:30em !important; height:20em !important;\"></canvas></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Graph 4</b>: Graph of the tangent function, redrawn here for comparison. Graph created with the <htcite0> library.</div></p><script> htPlotTan('charttan2', 1);</script>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "6efe7632-faed-4080-a5aa-38463d43e6d7",
                     "text": "Chart JS",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "05",
                        "day": "30"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### From one graph to the other\n\n**Graph 1** shows the secant in an intermediate position. We will now move the radius to the two extremes so we can understand the values that appear in **Graph 3**.\n\nWe start with the case where cos(θ) reaches its greatest value and, as a consequence, sec(θ) reaches its smallest:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p id=\"circtri3\"><style>.circle-draw circle, .circle-draw line {stroke: #71a6d2; stroke-width: 4; stroke-linecap: round; fill: none;} .circle-draw circle { stroke-dasharray: 942; stroke-dashoffset: 942; animation: drawCircle 2s linear forwards;} .radius-line { transform-origin: 300px 170px; animation: rotateRadius 2s linear forwards;} .radius-45 { opacity: 0; animation: showRadius45 0.3s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 2s; } .radius-30{ opacity: 0; animation: showRadius30 0.3s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 2s; } .vertical45 { opacity: 0; animation: showVertical45 0.3s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 2.5s; } .atlasTextRadius { opacity: 0; animation: atlasTextRadiusMov 0.3s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 2.8s; }</style><style>@keyframes drawCircle { to {stroke-dashoffset: 0; } } @keyframes rotateRadius { from { transform: rotate(0deg); } to   { transform: rotate(-360deg); } } @keyframes showRadius45 { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } } @keyframes showRadius30 { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } } @keyframes showVertical45 { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }  @keyframes atlasTextRadiusMov { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }</style><div class=\"atlasCircleContainer\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 340\" class=\"circle-draw\" id=\"svgcirctri0\">  <defs> <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"3\" markerHeight=\"3\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"> <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" /></marker> </defs> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"520\" y2=\"169\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"8\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"169\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"170\" r=\"148\" transform=\"scale(-1 1) translate(-600 0)  rotate(180 300 170)\"></circle> <line class=\"radius-line\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"448\" y2=\"169\"></line>  <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"360\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"350\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">sec θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"350\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">cos θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"282\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">O</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"282\" y=\"9\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">y</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"450\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">P</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"425\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"520\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">x</text></svg></div></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Graph 5</b>: Starting position: the radius lies on the x axis, so cos θ = 1 and sec θ = 1.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "As the radius begins to rotate upward, cos(θ) decreases toward zero. As a consequence, sec(θ) grows without bound. In the limit where cos(θ) approaches zero, the figure would look like **Graph 6**:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p id=\"circtri4\"><style>.circle-draw circle, .circle-draw line {stroke: #71a6d2; stroke-width: 4; stroke-linecap: round; fill: none;} .circle-draw circle { stroke-dasharray: 942; stroke-dashoffset: 942; animation: drawCircle 2s linear forwards;} .radius-line { transform-origin: 300px 170px; animation: rotateRadius 2s linear forwards;} .radius-45 { opacity: 0; animation: showRadius45 0.3s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 2s; } .radius-30{ opacity: 0; animation: showRadius30 0.3s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 2s; } .vertical45 { opacity: 0; animation: showVertical45 0.3s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 2.5s; } .atlasTextRadius { opacity: 0; animation: atlasTextRadiusMov 0.3s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 2.8s; }</style><style>@keyframes drawCircle { to {stroke-dashoffset: 0; } } @keyframes rotateRadius { from { transform: rotate(0deg); } to   { transform: rotate(-360deg); } } @keyframes showRadius45 { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } } @keyframes showRadius30 { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } } @keyframes showVertical45 { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }  @keyframes atlasTextRadiusMov { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }</style><div class=\"atlasCircleContainer\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 340\" class=\"circle-draw\" id=\"svgcirctri0\">  <defs> <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"3\" markerHeight=\"3\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"> <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" /></marker> </defs> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"520\" y2=\"169\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"8\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"169\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" style=\"stroke: black;\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"170\" r=\"148\" transform=\"scale(-1 1) translate(-600 0)  rotate(180 300 170)\"></circle>  <line class=\"radius-line\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"338\" y2=\"29\"></line> <line class=\"radius-line\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"169\" x2=\"868\" y2=\"169\"></line>  <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"360\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"325\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">cos θ</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"282\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">O</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"282\" y=\"9\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">y</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"450\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">P</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"425\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">Q</text> <text class=\"atlasTextRadius\" x=\"520\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"1.3em\" font-weight=\"bold\">x</text></svg></div></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Graph 6</b>: Limit case: as the radius rises, cos θ approaches 0 and the secant grows so long that its label leaves the figure.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "In this last graph we kept cos(θ) visible, but the secant has stretched so far that its label no longer fits in the figure.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### Practicing\n\nNow let us practice what we just learned. In **Graph 5**, the radius pointed to the right, where cos(θ) has its greatest value, 1, and — as a consequence — sec(θ) has its smallest value, also 1; tan(θ) is 0 there. That is exactly the starting position of the interactive app in **Graph 7**.\n\nClick on the chart to move the radius through the first quadrant. Watch the right triangle and θ change: as the radius rises from the horizontal, cos(θ) shrinks while sec(θ) and tan(θ) grow — just as **Graph 3** predicted and **Graph 6** illustrated. Try several positions and guess cos, sec, and tan before reading them in the panel under the chart.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"secPracticeInstruction\" style=\"text-align:center;\">Click on the chart to move the radius in the first quadrant. Watch cos(θ) shrink while sec(θ) and tan(θ) grow.</p> <div class=\"atlasCircleContainer\"><div id=\"secpractice520b\"></div></div> <p class=\"desc\"><b>Graph 7</b>: Interactive practice: as the radius moves through the first quadrant, cos(θ) shrinks while sec(θ) and tan(θ) grow.</p>",
               "source": [],
