               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nAlthough it is rarely used (<htcite0>), the secant deserves its place among the trigonometric functions. In this text we reviewed that sec(θ) = 1 / cos(θ): it equals 1 when cos(θ) = 1, grows as cos(θ) shrinks, and has no value where cos(θ) = 0 — the same behavior **Graph 3** and our interactive figure make visible.",
